Package: wayparam
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: fetch and normalize parameterized URLs from web archive indexes
 wayparam queries public web archive indexes, including the Internet Archive
 Wayback CDX API and Common Crawl CDXJ indexes, to retrieve historical URLs for
 a host (or a list of hosts), filters out common static/boring URLs, and
 outputs normalized URLs that contain query parameters.
 .
 By default query parameter values are replaced with a placeholder (FUZZ),
 which makes the output suitable for sharing and for fuzzing workflows.
 Historical modes can also summarize first/last seen timestamps, capture
 counts, status/MIME distributions and parameter prevalence. The tool does not
 crawl the target: it only queries public archive indexes, which makes it usable
 in passive OSINT and reconnaissance workflows.

Package: wayparam-gui
Architecture: all
Depends:
 wayparam (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: local web interface for wayparam
 wayparam collects historical URLs with query parameters from public archive
 indexes. This package adds wayparam-gui, which serves a small web interface on
 the loopback interface and streams results to the browser as they are found.
 .
 The interface binds to loopback only, requires a per-process random token on
 every request and rejects unexpected Host headers, because it performs
 outbound requests on behalf of whoever can reach it.
 .
 Install this package only if you want the interface: the wayparam command
 itself has no use for it.
